        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Point%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was founded in 1798 by William “Ranger” Davidson, making it one of Ohio’s oldest settlements.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.briggslibrary.org/content/south-point",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first church, First Baptist, began in 1823 and was originally organized at Stephen Ballard’s home on Solida Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
